<title>USA: Medquist approves 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Medquist approves 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>MARLTON, N.J. 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>MedQuist Inc said on Tuesday that its board of directors has declared a 3-for-2 stock split.</p>
<p>Shareholders will receive three common shares for every two shares of MedQuist common stock owned by shareholders of record as of August 25, 1997.</p>
<p>The shares will be issued on September 9, 1997, MedQuist said in a statement.</p>
<p>MedQuist currently has approximately 7.1 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Also, MedQuist said it has agreed to acquire Word Technologies Inc, an Atlanta-based medical transcription company with $2.2 million in 1996 revenues. Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Closing is scheduled for August 14. 1997.</p>
</text>
